WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.204 --> 00:00:00.999
Every January,

2
00:00:01.019 --> 00:00:03.395
Ohio State's staff gets about ten days to sort

3
00:00:03.415 --> 00:00:06.724
through thousands of names in the transfer portal,

4
00:00:06.744 --> 00:00:08.552
at every position on the field.

5
00:00:08.572 --> 00:00:12.885
Most of that work still happens in hallways, film rooms, and spreadsheets.

6
00:00:12.905 --> 00:00:14.659
Buckeye Edge changes that.

7
00:00:15.511 --> 00:00:19.126
Buckeye Edge is an advanced artificial intelligence decision system,

8
00:00:19.146 --> 00:00:20.889
built on agentic workflows.

9
00:00:20.909 --> 00:00:22.941
It senses what's happening in the portal,

10
00:00:22.961 --> 00:00:24.585
reasons over public data, film notes,

11
00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:27.087
and your staff's own grades,

12
00:00:27.107 --> 00:00:31.052
and delivers the answer to the right person, with the sources attached.

13
00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:32.864
Your coaches make the call.

14
00:00:32.884 --> 00:00:35.497
Every step the system takes is shown and logged.

15
00:00:36.299 --> 00:00:40.319
The work is done by the AI Workforce: a team of specialized agents.

16
00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.235
A Portal Scout watches for entries.

17
00:00:42.255 --> 00:00:44.571
A Carousel Watcher tracks coaching changes.

18
00:00:44.591 --> 00:00:46.875
A Film Analyst preps the film room.

19
00:00:46.895 --> 00:00:50.313
A Fit Scorer compares each player to your ideal profile.

20
00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:54.407
Others cover the market, compliance, the Monday brief, and fact-checking.

21
00:00:54.427 --> 00:00:56.823
Each one shows its steps, and its sources.

22
00:00:57.622 --> 00:00:59.038
Here's what that looks like.

23
00:00:59.058 --> 00:01:02.526
At six-oh-two in the morning, a cornerback enters the portal.

24
00:01:02.546 --> 00:01:04.128
The Portal Scout flags him.

25
00:01:04.148 --> 00:01:08.041
The Film Analyst pulls the clips to watch and the questions to settle.

26
00:01:08.061 --> 00:01:12.406
The Fit Scorer compares him to the three ideal corners your staff named.

27
00:01:12.426 --> 00:01:14.947
The Compliance Checker confirms the contact rules.

28
00:01:14.967 --> 00:01:18.486
And by six-nineteen, the defensive backs coach has a card on his phone:

29
00:01:18.506 --> 00:01:20.063
who he is, why he fits, and what to watch.

30
00:01:20.083 --> 00:01:24.173
The AI Workforce brings the work to your people.

31
00:01:24.193 --> 00:01:27.126
Anything that would contact a player waits for a named approval.

32
00:01:27.778 --> 00:01:31.644
And it runs at every position: quarterbacks, backs, receivers,

33
00:01:31.664 --> 00:01:35.397
tight ends, both lines, linebackers, the secondary, and specialists.

34
00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:37.762
Some positions have deeper data than others,

35
00:01:37.782 --> 00:01:42.908
so the system shows how much confidence it has at each one,

36
00:01:42.928 --> 00:01:45.963
right on the screen, and it gets sharper every season.

37
00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.114
How does it get sharper?

38
00:01:48.134 --> 00:01:52.902
Our methodology lead, Dr. Robert Rippee, points to four sources of variance.

39
00:01:52.922 --> 00:01:54.423
How people grade film.

40
00:01:54.443 --> 00:01:57.326
Program effects, when a player steps up to the Big Ten.

41
00:01:57.346 --> 00:02:00.503
Whether the measures themselves are reliable and valid.

42
00:02:00.523 --> 00:02:03.960
And outcomes, what actually happened to the players we rated.

43
00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:05.567
The system measures each one,

44
00:02:05.587 --> 00:02:08.805
and learns to explain more of the error, season after season.

45
00:02:09.535 --> 00:02:14.112
This year: a demo for the general manager and head coach before December,

46
00:02:14.132 --> 00:02:18.963
three ideal players named at every position, and the needs assessment.

47
00:02:18.983 --> 00:02:22.753
During the portal window, January fourth through the thirteenth,

48
00:02:22.773 --> 00:02:24.340
the AI Workforce runs live,

49
00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:29.603
and with permission, we record coaches thinking out loud in the film room.

50
00:02:29.623 --> 00:02:34.249
Year two: Ohio State's own standard measures at every position,

51
00:02:34.269 --> 00:02:37.923
program effects mapped, and checks against the 2024 and 2025 classes.

52
00:02:37.943 --> 00:02:41.824
Year three: computer-vision agents that grade film your way,

53
00:02:41.844 --> 00:02:45.623
and success forecasts, validated against real outcomes.

54
00:02:46.453 --> 00:02:50.561
It all starts with approvals: a sponsor, a data-sharing agreement,

55
00:02:50.581 --> 00:02:54.218
consent to record, and a privacy and compliance review.

56
00:02:54.238 --> 00:02:56.794
Dates stay open until they're signed.

57
00:02:56.814 --> 00:03:02.175
Open How It Works to meet the AI Workforce, take the tour, or just ask Edge.
